---
import Legal from '../../layouts/Legal.astro';
import { site } from '../../site';
---

<Legal
  lang="en"
  title="Terms of use"
  description="Terms for using Trakta: free, not tax advice, and without warranties."
  alternate="/villkor/"
>
  <div class="summary">
    <p>
      <strong>In short:</strong> Trakta is free and a helper, not tax advice. You are responsible for your own tax return
      and for checking the amounts.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2>About Trakta</h2>
  <p>
    Trakta is a free app that helps you keep track of per diem, business driving and commuting deductions in Sweden. It is
    developed as open source by {site.author} as a private individual. By using the app or this website you accept these
    terms.
  </p>

  <h2>Not tax advice</h2>
  <p>
    Trakta calculates with Skatteverket's published standard amounts and rules as I have interpreted them. The calculations
    may contain mistakes or be out of date, and your situation may differ from what the app assumes. Trakta is not tax
    advice and is not affiliated with Skatteverket (the Swedish Tax Agency).
  </p>

  <h2>Your responsibility</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>You are responsible for what you enter in your tax return. Check the amounts before you submit.</li>
    <li>Keep the records Skatteverket may ask for, such as receipts and your driving log.</li>
    <li>If you are unsure, read <a href="https://www.skatteverket.se" rel="noopener">skatteverket.se</a> or ask Skatteverket or a tax advisor.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Your data</h2>
  <p>
    Everything you enter is stored only on your phone (see the <a href="/en/privacy/">privacy policy</a>). You are
    responsible for backing up anything you want to keep. If you remove the app or lose your phone, the data is gone.
  </p>

  <h2>No warranty</h2>
  <p>
    The app and the website are provided as is, without warranties of any kind that they are error-free, complete or fit
    for a particular purpose.
  </p>

  <h2>Limitation of liability</h2>
  <p>
    To the extent permitted by law, I am not liable for any damage or loss arising from your use of the app or the
    website, such as incorrect figures in a tax return, tax surcharges or lost data. This does not limit any liability
    that cannot be limited under mandatory law.
  </p>

  <h2>Open source and licence</h2>
  <p>
    Trakta's source code is licensed under the <a href={`${site.repo}/blob/main/LICENSE`} rel="noopener">Apache License 2.0</a>.
    When you use, change or distribute the code, the licence applies, with its own disclaimer of warranty and limitation of
    liability.
  </p>
  <p>
    The licence gives no right to use the name Trakta, the logo or the app icon. They are covered by the
    <a href={site.trademarks} rel="noopener">trademark policy</a>.
  </p>
  <p>
    Builds made or distributed by others do not come from me. I only stand behind builds downloaded via trakta.app or from
    the <a href={site.releases} rel="noopener">releases of the GitHub project Dan-Irl/Trakta</a>, and the test version in
    Google Play.
  </p>

  <h2>Changes</h2>
  <p>
    The app may change, be updated or stop being developed. These terms may change; the latest version is always here,
    with the date at the top of the page.
  </p>

  <h2>Governing law</h2>
  <p>Swedish law applies to these terms.</p>

  <h2>Contact</h2>
  <p><a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></p>
</Legal>
